d stiff and solemn, as if dining in a mausoleum; the Earl of Carrington was also lifeless and gloomy. [1745] Bill Everly always looked hungrily at Virginia; George felt awkward in his position and tried to engage the baron and Mr. Isakov in conversation. [1746] The twins were lost in the joy of the commotion at home and had to be constantly restrained. Mr. Hale Fisk was slowly chewing his food and occasionally saying a few bland words in his usual slow, drawling manner. Sheriff Butler was nowhere to be seen, and no one knew his whereabouts. [1747] \"Thank God, we're done,\" Bunder muttered to Anthony as they left the table. \"George is going to bring the foreign delegation to the monastery this afternoon to discuss national affairs.\" [1748] \"That should help to lighten the mood,\" Anthony said approvingly. [1749] \"I don't mind the American,\" Bunder continued. \"He can have a quiet afternoon with his father talking about rare books.\" [1750] The American bowed deeply to her. [1751] \"You're too kind, Miss Erin,\" he said. [1752] \"Mr. Fischer has had a quiet morning,\" Anthony said. [1753] Mr. Fischer glanced at him quickly. [1754] \"Did you see me hiding in there? Sometimes, the only motto for a person who likes solitude is 'stay away from the crazy crowd.'\" [1755] \"Yes, there is,\" Anthony said. [1756] \"That bald guy is related to the family, too?\" [1757] \"Probably.\" [1758] \"These Central European countries are too chaotic,\" said Mr. Fitch. \"Is it true that the victim was a prince?\" [1759] \"He's staying here under the name of Count Stanislaus,\" Anthony said evasively. [1760] Mr. Fitch made no reply, but exclaimed mysteriously, \"My goodness!\" [1761] He then fell silent for a moment before speaking again. [1762] \"Is your constable, Batters or something, a crack shot?\" [1763] \"Scotland Yard thinks so,\" Anthony said coldly. [1764] \"I find him a bit conservative,\" Mr. Fitch said, \"lacking in initiative. What's the point of not allowing anyone to