ft after receiving the instructions. [1456] After a while, he returned with a person. The person was tall, with blond hair, high cheekbones, and deep blue eyes. His face was expressionless, almost matching Battert's. [1457] \"Are you Boris Anchukov?\" [1458] \"Yes.\" [1459] \"Are you the personal servant of Michael Prince?\" [1460] \"Yes.\" He spoke English well, but with a distinct foreign accent. [1461] \"Do you know that your master was murdered last night?\" [1462] The man did not answer, but only let out a wild animal-like howl. George jumped back, hastily retreating towards the window. [1463] \"Where was the last time you saw your master?\" [1464] \"The prince retired at ten o'clock. As usual, I slept in the small room next to his. He must have gone through another door to the rooms downstairs, the one on the corridor. I didn't hear him go out. Maybe I was drugged. I'm a negligent servant. My master is awake, and I'm sleeping. I should be damned.\" [1465] George stared at him intently, somewhat dazed. [1466] \"You have a lot of affection for your master?\" Batter asked, keeping a close eye on the other's movements. [1467] Baxter's face contorted with pain. He struggled to speak twice before his voice became shrill with emotion. [1468] \"British police, I tell you, I would die for him. Now he's dead, and I'm still alive, and if I don't avenge him, I'll die with my eyes closed and never find peace. I'll hunt down the murderer like a hound, and once I find him... Ah!\" He spoke with fire in his eyes. [1469] Suddenly, he pulled a large knife from his coat and waved it in the air. \"I won't kill him right away. No, I'll cut off his nose first, then chop off his ears, and gouge out his eyes. Then, I'll stab him in the heart with this knife!\" [1470] He turned and quickly put the knife back in its place, leaving the room. George stared intently at the door, which was now closed, and his already protruding eyes seemed ready to burst from their sockets. [1471] \"A true